DIVIDED-DIFFERENCE ADVERSARY REPORT FOR LP_exc^rel

0. UPFRONT VERDICT

Verdict: PARTIAL (local conditioning question REFUTED in the adversary's favor [proved + measured]; global confinement failure and sub-L[1/3] candidate yield NOT achieved, with N_ind = 0 across all 61 adversarial boxes at 84-112 bits [measured] and exponent c >= 1, alpha >= 1/3 [heuristic]).

Specifically, codex/dd_common.md:17-20 treats two statements for divided-difference modules of total pole degree p = O(m) as equivalent:
  (S1) forbidding conditioning loss log(M_i / t_i) ~ m log m at a positive fraction of the D embeddings;
  (S2) global threshold confinement Q := sum_{i=1}^D log t_i - log(N(c) N(c')) >= c_k x / T - C_k D m.
They are NOT equivalent [proved] (codex/scratch/dd_g/proofs.txt:41-84):
- Adversary win on (S1) [proved + measured]: Choosing linear poles R_j(T) = T - j (j = 1..m-2, p = m - 2), small base b, and P(T) = S(T) + R(T) U(T) with S(j) interpolating a scaled Alon-Vu / O_k-staircase inverse column y* = B^{-1} e_1 produces certified loss log(M_i / t_i) >= (m/2) log m - o(m log m) simultaneously at 4(n - m + 2) = (1 - (m - 2)/n) D embeddings while keeping irreducibility, linking, full k-rank m, and slow product growth s_h <= h(m - 1) + 1. At n = 12, m = 3..6, certified losses reach >= 0.75 m log m on 92%, 83%, 75%, and 67% of all D = 48 embeddings (codex/scratch/dd_g/results.json:3800-4660).
- Obstruction on (S2) and yield [proved + measured]: Achieving that simultaneous alignment forces root-pole scale separation rho >= exp(Omega(m log m)), which via the exact identity w_{2+j}(alpha_i) = prod_{l != i} (sigma(r_j) - alpha_l) inflates the 4(m - 2) pole-adjacent thresholds to Q >= Omega((1 - m/n) D m^2 log m) >> x / T [proved]. Conversely, minimizing pole remainders (P = 1 + R U, Family C1b) keeps H near the Theorem KH floor and drives Q = -10.3 < 0 even at 112 bits [measured], yet every full-support candidate still pays log|F| >= 1.24 log N (c = 1, alpha = 1/3) and yields N_ind = 0.

Environment and reproducibility: Repository .venv/bin/python3 provides mpmath, sympy, numpy, gmpy2, cypari2, and python-flint. All scratch files (prereg.txt, run_dd_adversary.py, proofs.txt, results.json, cyclotomic_supp.json, pell_poles_supp.json) reside in /Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/dd_g; repository files are untouched.


1. ADVERSARIAL CONSTRUCTIONS AND PRE-REGISTRATION

All experiments were pre-registered in codex/scratch/dd_g/prereg.txt:1-59 before running on 60-112 bit fixtures, using exact sweep.py parameters (experiments/chase/ch_L2c/sweep.py:89-91, 131): k = Q(sqrt(2)) (e = 2), N = a^2 - 2 from experiments/subthird/codex/experiment.py:28-43 (seeds 19 and 0), ternary box Omega = [-1, 1]^{2m}, cap = 3^{4n} 2^{ceil(bits/(2n))}, and B = 2^{ceil((bits * bit_length(bits-1)^3)^{1/4})}. Generators are w_1 = 1, w_2 = alpha, and w_{2+j} = (P // R_j)(alpha) = (sqrt(2) - (P mod R_j)(alpha)) / R_j(alpha) for pairwise coprime monic R_j of total degree p = O(m), with Q - P divisible by (T - b) prod_j R_j(T) so Q // R_j and P // R_j share identical evaluations mod N at T = b (experiments/chase/ch_L2c/proof.txt:129-141).

Six main families plus two supplementary pole families were tested (codex/scratch/dd_g/run_dd_adversary.py:157-395):
1. B0 (Control): Centered base-b P(b) = a with poles [T^2 + 1, T - 1, T + 1][:m-2] (experiment.py:55-83).
2. C1a (Base-b near-pole divisor alignment, exact P(b) = a): Linear poles R_j = T - (b - d_j) with d_j in {+-1, +-2} chosen so prod_j d_j > 0 divides a - c_0 for c_0 = +-1 (so P(r_j)^2 - 2 = -1 is a relative unit in O_k^*) and base-b U(T) in P = c_0 + R U.
3. C1b (Small-pole KH-floor unit-remainder family): Linear poles R_j = T - j (j = 1..m-2) with S(T) = 1 (P(j)^2 - 2 = -1) and P(b) = a + t N via centered base-b U(T) of degree n - m + 2, making prod_j R_j(alpha_i) ~ b^{-1} tiny at 4(m - 2) pole-clustered roots while minimizing H toward the Theorem KH floor (notes/subthird_results.md:27-36).
4. C2 (Totally-real scaled Chebyshev fields + root-clustered Chebyshev poles): P(T) = C_{n,L}(T - sh) + sum_{k<n} d_k C_{k,L}(T - sh) (where C_{n,L}(x) = 2 L^n T_n(x/(2L)) is monic in Z[x]) and Q = P + j_0(T - b) R, certified by Sturm counts to have all D = 4n roots real inside [sh - 2L, sh + 2L], paired with Chebyshev poles [X^2 - 2L^2, X - L, X + L][:m-2] (X = T - sh) inside the real root cluster.
5. C3_Z and C3_Ok (Alon-Vu and O_k-staircase residue-planted numerators): Linear poles R_j = T - j (j = 1..m-2), coupling m - 1 coordinates (w_2, ..., w_m) to an ill-conditioned ternary inverse column y* = B^{-1} e_1 over Z (C3_Z) or Z[sqrt(2)] (C3_Ok, where diag(-1+sqrt(2)) - subdiag(1+sqrt(2)) gives geometric ratio (1+sqrt(2))^2 = 5.828 per step plus ternary search) via S(j) approx -(x_0 - j) x_0 y*_{j+1} and U(T) = (T - x_0)^{n-m+2} + c_lin(T - b) - M_2 with b = x_0 + d_b and x_0 >= 8 m^2 ||y*||_inf M_2^{1/(n-m+2)}.
6. Supplementary C_cyc and C_pell (codex/scratch/dd_g/cyclotomic_supp.json:1-77, pell_poles_supp.json:1-26): Cyclotomic unit-circle poles [Phi_3, Phi_6] = [T^2+T+1, T^2-T+1] with S = 1 (achieving min |prod R_j(alpha_i)| = 3e-6 and |prod R_j| < 0.1 at 16/36 = 44% of embeddings), and quadratic Z[T] minimal polynomials of Pell-unit multiples j(sqrt(2) - 1)^K.

Disclosed execution adjustments: Strict prefix spaces use dim_k < m (matching experiments/masullo_ext/mext_c/cover.py:69 when ternary vectors tie at t_i); C3 couples m - 1 generators around real center x_0 with adaptive 512/1024-bit ball precision; pre-registered sub-prediction P2 that C2 would keep Q < 0 was falsified because matching P(b) = a with 2n real roots forces Chebyshev scale L ~ b/2, inflating H (whereas C1b achieved Q < 0 up to 112 bits).


2. MEASURED CONDITIONING LOSS AND CANDIDATE COUNTS (60-112 BITS)

All thresholds M_i, t_i, H, and Q are certified with 512- to 1024-bit flint arb/acb ball arithmetic; all norms F and prime-ideal valuation parities use exact flint resultants and PARI nfinit/idealprimedec (codex/scratch/dd_g/run_dd_adversary.py:398-695). Every run verified slow product growth s_h = h(p + 1) + 1 up to 2n.

