Across all 54 main boxes at 84, 96, and 112 bits plus 7 cyclotomic/Pell boxes, full-support capped candidates equal 0 and N_ind = 0 under every quotient definition. Even at 60 and 72 bits (B0 seed 19), the 3 and 1 coordinate-full rows lie inside a single non-coordinate prefix hyperplane (N_ind_prefix = 0, matching chase_L2_codex.out:3). In C1b, capped orbits triple to 78-84, yet all lie in proper k-subspaces of rank <= m - 1.


3. EXPONENT LEDGER IF SCALED

Using the repository ledger d = x^delta, r = e m = x^rho, log B = x^alpha, cost L[alpha] => rho = alpha, and log X = x^{1 + c*rho - delta} + 2 d log 3, smoothness feasibility u log u <= C yields alpha = 1 / (4 - c) [proved arithmetic; heuristic endpoints] (src/grdeg/ledger.py:37-101, notes/grdeg_results.md:34-42):
- Hypothetical sub-1/3 target (c = 0): log|F| ~ x/d + O(d), delta = 1/2, alpha = 1/4 (requires N_ind >= pi(B)/rho(u) outside proper k-subspaces).
- C1a, C1b, C_cyc (KH-floor small pole remainders |S_j| = O(1)) [heuristic]: Full-support candidates have deg N_a = p + 1 >= m - 1 roots of O(1) modulus away from R = 0 where |P(xi) - sqrt(2)|, |Q(xi) - sqrt(2)| ~ b, giving |F(a)| ~ b^{4(p+1)} >= N^{2(m-1)/n} (exact-a) or N^{4(m-1)/(n-m+2)} (general-N linking). Here log|F| ~ (r/d) x => c = 1, delta = 2/3, alpha = 1/3 (confirmed by measured minFull/lnN = 1.24 at (12,4) vs 4*3/10 = 1.20, and 2.24 at (12,5) vs 4*4/9 = 1.78).
- B0 (standard base-b remainders |S_j| ~ b) [heuristic]: Newton polygon of N_a gives two roots of modulus ~ b^{1/2}, yielding full-support |F(a)| ~ b^{4(n-1)} ~ N^2 (general N: N^4), i.e., log|F| = Theta(x), giving L[1/2].
- C2 (totally-real Chebyshev, L ~ b/2), C3 (Alon-Vu planted numerators), C_pell [proved + heuristic]: log|F| = Theta(r x) >> x, worse than L[1/2].


4. STRONGEST OBSTRUCTIONS PROVED

Full proofs are in codex/scratch/dd_g/proofs.txt:3-129:

1. Trivial generator ideal, shared-denominator cancellation, and pole-proximity anti-loss [proved] (proofs.txt:13-39):
   (a) Monic R_j in O_k[T] forces w_{2+j} = (P // R_j)(alpha) in O_K; with w_1 = 1, c = O_K, c' = O_{K'}, so J = N(c)N(c') = 1, H = sum log M_i >= sum log^+|alpha_i| >= 0, and Q = sum log t_i.
   (b) Multiplying w(alpha_i) by sigma(R)(alpha_i) scales M_i and t_i by the exact same factor |sigma(R)(alpha_i)|, so a tiny shared denominator prod_j R_j(alpha_i) cancels identically out of M_i / t_i.
   (c) Whenever one generator dominates at embedding i (max_{k != k_0} |L_i(w_k)| <= (c_min / (2 m C_sigma)) M_i, as near any simple pole root), every full-rank ternary basis contains a row with a_{k_0} != 0, forcing t_i > (c_min / 2) M_i and log(M_i / t_i) < log(2 / (sqrt(2) - 1)) = 1.575 (observed in C_cyc and C3's 0.88 floor).

2. Linear-pole product identity vs Alon-Vu alignment [proved] (proofs.txt:41-84):
   For R_j = T - r_j, dividing sigma(P)(sigma(r_j)) - sigma(sqrt(2)) = prod_{l=1}^n (sigma(r_j) - alpha_l) by sigma(r_j) - alpha_i yields the exact identity
     w_{2+j}(alpha_i) = prod_{l != i} (sigma(r_j) - alpha_l).
   Any construction (such as C3 or O_k-unit-clustered poles) separating Theta(n) roots from m - 2 poles by scale K_m = exp(Omega(m log m)) at some base place sigma forces the pole-adjacent embeddings to pay |w_{2+j}(alpha_*)| >= (c K_m)^{Theta(n)} with single-coordinate dominance (Lemma 1c), driving Q >= Omega(D m^2 log m) >> x / T.

3. Singular-value concentration, real-root pigeonhole cap, and same-numerator resultant law [proved + heuristic] (proofs.txt:86-129):
   (a) [proved] For any invertible A in A^{m x m}, ||sigma(A)||_F <= C_k m and |det sigma(A)| >= (C_k sqrt(m))^{-(e-1)m} imply prod_{l=1}^q sigma_l(sigma(A)) >= e^{-q/2} C_k^{-em+q} m^{-(em-q)/2}. Taking q = ceil((e + 2)/gamma) = O_{k,gamma}(1) gives sigma_q > m^{-gamma m / 2}, confining gamma-ill-conditioned unit vectors to radius m^{-gamma m / 2 + 1/2} around a (q - 1)-dimensional subspace E_A (covering number exp(O_k(m^2)) across all <= 3^{em^2} matrices). At near-maximal loss gamma = e/2 - o(1) (q = 2), dim E_A = 1, so any two embeddings sharing A suffer cross-ratio collapse |(r_{j_1}-r_{j_2})(alpha_1-alpha_2)/((alpha_1-r_{j_1})(alpha_2-r_{j_2}))| <= m^{-Omega(m)}, triggering Obstruction 2. Meanwhile, generic real embeddings only pack 3^{em} points into R^1, capping generic real loss at (e log 3) m + O_k(log m) = O_k(m) [proved].
   (b) [proved identity] Because Q - P = (T - b) R(T) Delta(T), BOTH sides share the identical cleared numerator polynomial N_a(T) of degree d_a <= p + 1 and identical pole resultant Delta_R = Res_T(P - sqrt(2), R), satisfying Res_T(Q - P, N_a) = (-1)^{d_a} N_a(b) (prod_j c_j^{deg R_j}) (+-Delta_R) (prod_{j!=l} Res_T(R_j, R_l)) Res_T(Delta, N_a). Full-support vectors have c_j != 0 and d_a = p + 1 >= m - 1, preventing pole cancellation and forcing c >= 1 [heuristic].


5. NEXT STEP

Switch to the prover side on the sole remaining gap in codex/dd_common.md:18: C3 proves (S1) is false as a blanket local statement, so a proof of (S2) must use H = O_k(D m log m) (which bounds sum_i log^+|alpha_i| and pole heights) together with Theorem 3(a)'s q = O_{k,gamma}(1) subspace bound. Specifically, prove by resultant/Bezout elimination along the degree-(p + 1) polynomial curve alpha |-> [N(alpha)] in P^{m-1}(C) that hitting distinct (q - 1)-dimensional subspaces E_{A^(i)} at >= C_{k,gamma} m well-separated roots forces coefficient height of N(T) — and hence pole-adjacent thresholds via Obstruction 2 — above Omega(D m^2 log m), closing Q >= c_k x / T - C_k D m unconditionally for divided-difference modules.
